ine Public", "published": "2026-10-07T11:11:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxOdUZheXdmVU9NSDFCbm5BSnBiclZBLWNrMDIyN0Z3QThtaWNFd0tBZThjR0FGcXkzbHdVLVBONC1nSnh6ckhGYWVXbjVld2poOUREMG9hZlhMZmUyY29YUTFHQ2lPVFhldmJtZllYNFVCUTNBYnRNTmhFUnNpTzRyVEhBSEZnT1BFN25CNnZJN09fcmRSQWlHb01YcjJYb3JDTWM5TTJzNGd2NmVsckRGQW8tYTJKR0RWVnRkVXNMcjBZR1lQ?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 3.95, "prior_sd": 5.0, "poll_margin": 2.48, "poll_sd": 4.37, "poll_weight": 0.57, "fundamentals": {"margin": 6.89, "lean": 4.0, "environment": 7.56, "incumbency": -3.0, "money": -1.67}, "rating_margin": 2.0, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 6.21, "baseline_margin": 3.12, "analyst_adjustment": -0.62, "key_factors": ["Recent polls consistently show Jackson narrowly ahead, including high-quality surveys from WaPo/SSPG, Marist and UNH", "Collins's incumbency and $11M cash advantage partially offset a favorable Democratic environment in a state with a D+4 lean", "Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean D, with markets pricing Jackson around 55-58%", "Collins's long history of outperforming her polls adds uncertainty"], "rationale": "Polling since late September shows Jackson with a small but consistent lead, averaging around two points, and markets and several modelers lean Democratic. Collins's incumbency, fundraising edge and history of beating expectations keep this short of Likely D.", "watch": "A late shift toward Collins among independents, or a polling miss in her favor as in past cycles, would move this back to Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Susan Collins (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Maine's Senate race pits six-term incumbent Susan Collins against state Democrat Troy Jackson in one of the closest contests of the cycle. Polls since late September mostly show Jackson ahead by one to four points, though some Republican-leaning pollsters have it tied or Collins up slightly. The state's D+4 lean and a favorable national environment for Democrats cut against Collins, but her incumbency, name recognition and large fundraising edge keep her competitive.\n\nExpert raters are split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets give Jackson roughly a 55-58% chance. Collins has worked to distance herself from Trump, and her history of outperforming polls looms over the final stretch. The race remains genuinely competitive, with a modest Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7341, "margin": 3.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6906, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.626, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6915, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5751, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6474, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6668, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6495, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6994, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6388, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6279, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5727, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6061, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6059, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6373, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6384, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6413, "margin": 2.5}]}